The darkness retreated. For the first time, the world knew dawn.

The people wept with joy, but when they climbed the mountain to thank her, they found only her empty loom. Some say Alara became the dawn itself, her patient weaving creating each new sunrise.

Now, every morning, the sky glows golden—a reminder that even in deepest darkness, persistent hope can weave light.
